On making wizards able to permanently memorize spells:

Certainly the current system is ridiculous - when did you last say
"Oh no, I'm low on energy points, better drink a potion of gain energy?"
But I don't think this is the way to fix it. Why would one find GRAY
dragons particularly? (Yes, I see why it's necessary for this process,
but it doesn't make game sense.)

I think the thing that wizards should get is the ability to see how +
an item is, like priest's ability to see blessed/cursed. It needn't
work on items that are -.

For that matter, priests are too powerful in this way. Idea:
have priests come in lawful and chaotic varieties, and only be able to tell
if an item is of their alignment. Responses?
